@@ -70,6 +70,12 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result as plain text followed by ``end``. It does not pretty print containers, does not wrap or crop text to the console width, does not apply markup, and does not replace emoji codes. It does apply highlighting (on by default) and an optional basic ``style``. Use ``out`` when you want raw text written as-is, rather than rich's formatting.
+
+
